---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'Zodiacs AI Integrations | Zodiacs.org';
const description = 'Connect an AI assistant to the hosted Zodiacs MCP server or the local developer plugin: supported tools, privacy and installation.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/developers/ai/">
  <section class="section container container--narrow ai-page">
    <em class="kicker">Developer tools</em>
    <h1 class="display">Build with the sky</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Zodiacs connects AI assistants to the Zodiacs engine in two ways: a hosted MCP server at <code>https://zodiacs.org/mcp</code> for any assistant that accepts remote MCP connections, and a local developer plugin that runs on your own machine. Public directory listings remain release gates.</p>
      <h2>Connect it</h2>
      <p>The hosted server needs no account, sign-in or key. In Claude, open Customize, then Connectors, add a custom connector and enter <code>https://zodiacs.org/mcp</code>. Other assistants that accept remote MCP connections use the same address. Then ask one of the questions below.</p>
      <h2>The hosted server</h2>
      <p>The hosted server computes positions at an explicit instant, finds sign ingresses, stations and new/full Moons in a window of up to 92 days, and checks astronomical claims. Answers include UTC, a display timezone, calculation receipts and numerical limits. A date-only claim can return <code>depends</code>. Event-search completeness is tested, not proven.</p>
      <p>It also serves dated Sun-sign horoscopes from the site's daily edition. It keeps the editions for the day before, the day of and the day after, so a reader in any time zone gets the reading written for their own date. Horoscopes are interpretation, for reflection.</p>
      <p>Its sky calendar, horoscope panel and Chart Studio declare sidebar and conversation-panel entrypoints. Chart Studio asks for birth details inside its panel and calculates there; the assistant receives only a selection the person reviews and shares. The server offers no birth-chart storage, scheduling, eclipse search or predictions of personal outcomes.</p>
      <p>Ask “What changes this week in Bangkok?”, “Is Mercury retrograde right now?” or “Show today's horoscope for Leo.” An answer should be useful in the conversation. Links to the <a href="/moon-phase/">Moon tool</a>, <a href="/full-moon-calendar/">lunar calendar</a> and <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> offer optional further exploration.</p>
      <h2>Build and verify an integration</h2>
      <p>Zodiacs Developer provides skills for building with the engine, checking output and testing an integration. Its local stdio server adds natal-chart calculation and record comparison to the public-sky tools. It opens no listener or outbound connection. The <a href="/developers/mcp/">existing local MCP adapter</a> remains available separately.</p>
      <p>In a checkout, run <code>npm ci</code> and <code>npm test</code> in <code>plugins/zodiacs-developer</code>. The plugin contains pinned dependencies, three skills and runnable synthetic sky/calendar examples. Installation details and review evidence are in the <a href="https://github.com/zodiacs-org/site/tree/main/plugins/zodiacs-developer">plugin directory</a>.</p>
      <h2>What local means</h2>
      <p>The developer server computes on its machine. The assistant provider can still receive the arguments and results. Hosted sky calculations run on Zodiacs infrastructure. Public-sky tools need no birth details; derived natal positions remain personal data. Read the <a href="/privacy/#ai-integrations">AI integration privacy explanation</a> before connecting personal records.</p>
      <p>Use the published <a href="/developers/engine/">calculation engine</a> in external projects and preserve its notices. Site-derived candidate code retains the site's license. A receipt supports reproduction; it does not certify an imported record's authenticity or validate astrological interpretation.</p>
      <p>For current support and known calculation limitations, see <a href="/developers/support/">developer support</a> and <a href="/developers/conformance/">independent-reference conformance</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .ai-page h1 { margin: var(--s-3) 0 var(--s-6); }
  .ai-page h2 { margin-top: var(--s-10); font-size: var(--text-lg); }
  .ai-page code { font-family: var(--font-mono); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
